  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2227$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $10$ is composite or even. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{10\\text{\u00a0is composite}}_{\u23df}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{10\\text{\u00a0is even\u00a0}}_{\u23df}}_{B}\n$$\n\nthat is, $A\u2228B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $8$ is divisible by $2$ or $6.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{8\\text{\u00a0is divisible by 2}}_{\u23df}}_{C}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{8\\text{\u00a0is divisible by\u00a0}6}_{\u23df}}_{D},\n$$\n\nthat is, $C\u2228D.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{10\\text{\u00a0is composite\u00a0}\\text{or}\\text{\u00a0even}}_{\u23df}}_{A\\,\u2228\\,B}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{8\\text{\u00a0is divisible by\u00a0}2\\text{\u00a0or\u00a0}6}_{\u23df}}_{C\\,\u2228\\,D},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(A\u2228B)\u2227(C\u2228D).$",
